---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import products from '../../data/products.json';
import '../../styles/buyer-content.css';
const examples = products.filter(p => ['multi-head','compact-wall','garden-spot'].includes(p.id));
---
<BaseLayout title="How to select solar outdoor lights for B2B orders | NICETHRYUN" description="A practical solar-lighting buyer guide: panel placement, motion modes, fixture dimensions, sample checks and the information needed for a quotation.">
<header class="page-header"><div class="page-header-inner"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/resources/">Resources</a><span aria-current="page">Solar lighting selection</span></nav><p class="eyebrow blue-text">BUYER GUIDE</p><h1>How to select<br />solar outdoor lights.</h1><p>For distributors, private-label brands and property buyers: start with the installation, compare the configuration, then approve a sample.</p><p class="buyer-meta">NICETHRYUN · Updated <time datetime="2026-11-19">19 November 2026</time></p></div></header>
<article class="buyer-content"><nav class="buyer-content__toc" aria-label="Guide contents"><a href="#panel-placement">Panel placement</a><a href="#operation">Night-time use</a><a href="#dimensions">Real dimensions</a><a href="#sample-checks">Sample checks</a><a href="#quote-brief">Quotation brief</a></nav>
<section id="panel-placement"><h2>Integrated or separate solar panel?</h2><p><strong>Choose the panel arrangement around the available sunlight.</strong> An integrated unit places the panel and light together. A separate panel allows different mounting positions; cable length, connections and routing then become part of the selection.</p><div class="buyer-content__table"><table><thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Integrated format</th><th>Separate-panel format</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Where can the panel face daylight?</th><td>Assess the light's mounting position and nearby shade.</td><td>Identify a separate panel position and confirm the cable reaches it.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">What should the sample confirm?</th><td>Panel exposure, head adjustment, fixing and operating mode.</td><td>Those points plus connectors, cable protection and panel fixing.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Formats to compare</th><td><a href="/products/multi-head/">Three-head sensor light</a> and <a href="/products/compact-wall/">compact wall light</a></td><td><a href="/products/split-panel/">Split-panel security light</a> and <a href="/products/garden-spot/">sheltered patio pendant</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Share a photograph showing the proposed position, roof edges, trees and other potential shade.</p></section>
<section id="operation"><h2>Define what the light should do at night.</h2><p><strong>State the operating mode and required hours before comparing runtime claims.</strong> Motion-to-off, motion-to-dim and constant illumination are different requirements. Confirm which modes the selected model provides and how each was tested.</p><p>Solar lighting depends on available solar energy and battery storage. Seasonal exposure and reduced charging conditions matter when assessing an operating schedule. The US Department of Energy's <a href="https://betterbuildingssolutioncenter.energy.gov/resources/solar-powered-street-and-area-lighting-considerations-fact-sheet">solar-powered lighting considerations</a> explains these general system factors; it is not test evidence for a NICETHRYUN model.</p><ul><li>Give the destination and photographs of panel exposure.</li><li>Describe nightly hours, light colour and motion behaviour.</li><li>Request the configuration's test conditions and results. LED count and concept imagery do not establish measured coverage.</li></ul></section>
<section id="dimensions"><h2>Check the fixture's actual dimensions.</h2><p><strong>Compare the lamp dimensions with the wall, door or mounting surface.</strong> A close-up photograph does not establish real-world scale. These examples use the same supplier data as the product pages.</p><div class="buyer-content__table"><table><thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Listed dimension</th><th>Size</th></tr></thead><tbody>{examples.map(p => { const size = p.specs.find(([label]) => label.startsWith('Product size'))!; return <tr><td><a href={`/products/${p.id}/`}>{p.name}</a></td><td>{size[0]}</td><td>{size[1]}</td></tr>; })}</tbody></table></div><p class="buyer-content__note">Supplier-listed values require sample confirmation. They are not independent test results. Missing lamp dimensions remain unconfirmed; packaging dimensions are not substituted.</p></section>
<section id="sample-checks"><h2>What should a B2B sample check include?</h2><ul><li><strong>Identity:</strong> match the sample, model reference, photographs and written specification.</li><li><strong>Installation:</strong> inspect dimensions, hardware, panel position, connectors and maintenance access.</li><li><strong>Operation:</strong> check light colour, controls and sensor behaviour under agreed conditions.</li><li><strong>Evidence:</strong> request output, runtime, enclosure and battery information for the quoted configuration. A catalogue badge alone does not establish certification.</li><li><strong>Agreement:</strong> confirm packaging, instruction language, sample approval, inspection and after-sales terms in writing.</li></ul><p>Destination requirements depend on the product and market. Confirm the required documents with the supplier and relevant import or compliance adviser before purchase.</p></section>
<section id="quote-brief"><h2>Send a brief that can be quoted.</h2><p><strong>Include product links, quantity, destination and installation requirements in one request.</strong> Add sample needs and private-label requirements so configuration and commercial terms can be discussed together.</p><ul><li>Company, business email, destination and buyer role.</li><li>Product links, order and sample quantities, and target timing.</li><li>Site dimensions, mounting height, panel exposure and operating schedule.</li><li>Packaging, logo, language and document requirements.</li></ul><p>Price, MOQ, lead time and suitability are confirmed for the agreed scope. A downloaded brief or saved draft is not a submitted inquiry; check the form's submission result.</p><div class="buyer-content__actions"><a class="btn btn-blue" href="/inquiry/">Prepare your inquiry ↗</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/downloads/selection-checklist.txt" download>Download the checklist</a><a class="btn btn-outline" href="/products/">Compare products</a></div></section>
</article></BaseLayout>
